     <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
     <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
     <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+
+    <h2>4. Data minimization and third parties</h2>
+    <p><strong>Reading list</strong></p>
+    <p>A session cookie is only created when you save an article to your reading list. It stores the list of article identifiers, nothing else, and is not shared with third parties.</p>
+    <p><strong>Analytics</strong></p>
+    <p>Third-party analytics is disabled by default. It is loaded only if you click “Accept” in the consent banner, and never if your browser sends a Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track signal. You can withdraw consent by clearing this site's local storage.</p>
+    <p><strong>Sign in and sign up</strong></p>
+    <p>Your username and password are sent over HTTPS to our authentication service and are not stored in your browser or logged by this website.</p>
+    <p><strong>Fonts</strong></p>
+    <p>Fonts are loaded from Google Fonts without referrer information.</p>
+    <p><strong>Security</strong></p>
+    <p>This site enforces a strict Content Security Policy, HSTS and related headers, and restricts which third-party origins can run code or receive data. Third-party integrations are reviewed regularly; see our audit record in the project repository.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
